-- title:
--   A Γ₀(M)-action on the q-expansion function field of X_H
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $M$ a positive natural number with $M \neq 0$ in $K$, and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$; write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the set of $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower right entry reduces into $H$. For a subgroup $\Gamma$ of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) is the intermediate field of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by all quotients $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one common weight for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are integral power series whose complex reductions are the width-one $q$-expansions of $f,g$, $\bar p$ denotes the Laurent series obtained by reducing coefficients into $K$, and $\bar p_g \neq 0$. The assertion is that there exists a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(M)$ to the group of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F_H :=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (GammaH M H)` such that: $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(M)$; $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ when $\gamma = -1$; every $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes each element of $F_H$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC K (Gamma0 M)`; and, for every $\gamma$, every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ and every $c \in \mathbb{C}^\times$ with $f_1 = c\,(f\mid_k\gamma)$ and $g_1 = c\,(g\mid_k\gamma)$ as functions on $\mathbb{H}$, and with $\bar p_g \neq 0 \neq \bar p_{g_1}$, one has $\rho(\gamma)(\bar p_f/\bar p_g) = \bar p_{f_1}/\bar p_{g_1}$ in $K((q))$.
--
--   This is the diamond action of $\Gamma_0(M)/\Gamma_H(M)\{\pm 1\}$ on the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(M)$, realised over an arbitrary field in which $M$ is invertible, together with the compatibility that pins the action down on ratios of integral $q$-expansions. It underlies the comparison of the fields attached to $\Gamma_1(M)$ and $\Gamma_0(M)$ (faithfulness of the action, fixed field, and degree equal to the index) and the surjectivity statements for the Hecke and diamond generators used later.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_monoidHom_gamma0_algEquiv_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH.lean

